  "content": {
    "id": "v2-11f0f-p40-practice-retro-slot-2-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "A child in a Perth backyard throws a ball that follows the path $y=-0.05x^2+x+1$, where $y$ is the height above the ground, in metres, and $x$ is the horizontal distance from the child, in metres. The sloping roof of a shed lies along the line $y=0.4x+2.5$.\nDetermine whether the ball will hit the roof.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Yes. Setting $0.4x+2.5=-0.05x^2+x+1$ gives $\\Delta=0.06>0$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}0.4x+2.5&=-0.05x^2+x+1\\\\0.05x^2-0.6x+1.5&=0\\\\\\Delta&=(-0.6)^2-4(0.05)(1.5)\\\\\\Delta&=0.06>0\\end{align*}$$\nThere are two real intersections, so the path meets the line of the roof and the ball hits the roof.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 50
  },
